        "text": "The Hebrew word {original} covers wind, breath and spirit (see its lexicon range). The Septuagint has {lxx} and the Vulgate {vulgate}, both able to mean breath or spirit; WEBC capitalises it as \"{webc}\". Whether the verse speaks of a wind from God or of God's Spirit is a matter of reading.",
